From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arr-optimized <arr-optimized@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Bound the housekeeping wait, forget replaced files'
 ffprobe results, copy release profiles

- Housekeeping still waits until no other command runs, but only for
  HousekeepingCommand.MaxDeferral (30 minutes) after it was queued. After
  that it starts like stock: alongside the running commands and not
  exclusive, so a stuck or very long command cannot keep housekeeping from
  running forever. A waiting consumer re-checks the queue when the wait
  runs out. The wait is logged once at Debug, and an overdue housekeeping
  that starts alongside other commands is logged at Info.
- Importing, deleting or renaming a movie file drops the ffprobe cache
  entries for the paths involved, so with "Change File Date" an upgrade at
  the same path with the same size does not get the old file's media info.
  A probe that overlapped such an invalidation is not stored.
- The release profile service hands out copies of the cached profiles, so
  a caller that changes a returned profile cannot change what later
  callers see (stock read new objects from the database on every call).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
